# CS-530 2D Game: Starfall Arena

**Starfall Arena** is a compact local two-player arcade-fighter engine inspired by the speed, air mobility, and dramatic knockback of classic team-based arcade fighters. It intentionally uses original geometry-based fighters rather than third-party character assets.

The playable foundation includes a deterministic 60 Hz simulation, walking and jumping, buffered light/heavy attacks, hitboxes, hitstun, launch knockback, health bars, rounds, and first-to-two match flow. The render layer is separate from combat rules, making character animation, special moves, assists, throws, and rollback networking natural future extensions.

## Run it

Requires Python 3.10 or newer.

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python3 -m pip install -e .
python3 -m starfall
```

## Controls

| Action | Control |
| --- | --- |
| Player 1 move / jump | A/D, W |
| Player 1 light / heavy | F, G |
| Player 2 move / jump | Left/Right arrows, Up arrow |
| Player 2 light / heavy | K, L |
| Restart after match | F or K |
| Quit | Close the window |

The game runs at a 960×540 window resolution. Combat uses a fixed 60 Hz update while rendering can run independently, and the rules live in `src/starfall/game.py` so they can be tested without opening a graphical window.

## Development

```bash
PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest discover -s tests
```

## Project layout

```text
src/starfall/game.py  # Testable fixed-step combat and match rules
src/starfall/app.py   # Pygame input, stage drawing, and fixed-step loop
tests/test_game.py    # Headless gameplay-rule tests
```
